@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: WWW Redirects
	Frontend testing for creating an www source links

Setup:
    * I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I sign out and sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	* I tear down the links with the folowing source url and destination url values
	| privacy | https://www.liferay.com/privacy-policy |

Scenario: Add Source Link
	Admins should be able to add a source link on www.

	Given I go to the www homepage
	And I click on the Sign In Create Account footer link
	And I sign into www as a user with the email address "${staticWWWAdminEmailAddress}" and password "${staticWWWAdminPassword}"
	And I navigate to the Product Menu and go to the "Redirection" portlet under the "Configuration" category under the "Site Administration" panel
	And I click on the add button in the redirection page
	And I create a source link with the following values
	| Source URL      | Input  | privacy                                |
	| Destination URL | Input  | https://www.liferay.com/privacy-policy |
	| Type            | Select | Temporary (302)                        |
    And I go to the www page with the url "privacy"
    Then the current url content should contain the text "privacy-policy"